To Whom It May Concern:

Patient: {{Patient.Name}} (Member ID {{Patient.MemberID}})
Claim #: {{Claim.Number}}  |  CPT {{Claim.CPT}}  |  Date of Service: {{Claim.ServiceDate}}
Rendering Provider: {{Provider.Name}}  |  NPI: {{Provider.NPI}}
Diagnosis Code(s): {{Claim.DiagnosisCodes}}

We are appealing the denial of CPT 11970 on the basis that the billed diagnosis code(s) are inconsistent with the procedure performed. The diagnosis code(s) submitted, {{Claim.DiagnosisCodes}}, correctly reflect [DESCRIBE: e.g. encounter for prophylactic/post-mastectomy breast reconstruction (Z42.1) together with the patient's personal history of mastectomy], which is the standard and appropriate diagnosis coding for a staged expander-to-implant exchange — this is not a mismatch, but the clinically correct pairing for this reconstructive stage.

We respectfully request that {{Payer.Name}}:
• Review the diagnosis code(s) submitted against the clinical documentation confirming the reconstructive indication.
• Overturn the denial and reprocess CPT 11970 for payment.

We expect a formal redetermination within standard appeal timelines. For any immediate clinical or administrative inquiries regarding this appeal, contact {{Sender.Name}} directly at {{Sender.Email}} or {{Sender.Phone}}.
